5	Division A: Communicative Networks and Informative Platforms
6	UNTITLED S CORP
7	LLC 1: WAV : A New Way To Listen.
8	WAV is a live map that lets you see music that’s being played by those nearby you. Allowing you to
9	find music and people unique to you by sending and receiving music requests from profiles you know or
10	like, letting you know who’s got the best taste in music that you listen to. WAV lets you create a playlist
11	called a WAV Radio, containing songs from separate music streaming platforms such as Spotify, Apple
12	Music, Pandora, Soundcloud, etc. Keeping your songs in one playlist instead of hopping platforms to find
13	the songs you like for the people you love. WAV accounts also have the option to integrate multimedia
14	platforms such as Instagram or YouTube if an artist is looking to share their music and other types of media
15	on the WAV. As the WAV expands, artists, advertisers, and mass media outlets can study the WAV to
16	measure, identify and predict music taste, market behaviors, and social preferences on a geographical
17	scale. Most importantly, WAV accounts have the option to stay out of the WAV in order to protect a user's
18	privacy. Allowing you to ride the WAV without being eaten by the sharks.
19	
20	LLC 2: LINK : Stay In Touch.
21	Link is a proprietary NFC tag that can be worn discreetly as a piece of jewelry or body piercing.
22	With proprietary designs made to appear like ‘the real deal’, Link allows users to exchange data
23	and contacts without the worry of unwanted attention from third parties. Without accounts sign-ups or user
24	info, Link users can enjoy data exchanges without the worry of data compromises or extortions as seen
25	from other companies such as Ashley Madison or Tinder, all while keeping track of exchanges and contacts
26	using the Link app. Link also allows wearers to integrate the proprietary NFC to their own jewelry and
27	piercings of choice for a more subtle approach. Potential collaborations include Hybrid Body Lab, MIT
28	Media Lab, Microsoft Research team’s DUOSKIN with the goal to develop a more discreet and biological
29	NFC integrated tattoo and communication device.
30	
31	LLC 3: WINK : For Telepaths.
32	Wink is the world’s first brain-computer interface dating app hosted by Neuralink and Blackrock Neurotech
33	aimed to allow users to send winks telepathically and anonymously. Allowing users to exchange ‘Winks’ and
34	contacts without the worry of receiving unwanted attention. As users interact via Wink, contacts and data
35	are discreetly stored in the users BCI without the need to sign up for any accounts that are prone to data
36	breaches.
37	
38	LLC 4: SYNC : A New Way To Connect.
39	Sync is an artificially intelligent significant other with wireless compatibility in health and
40	wellness products of your choosing. Sync allows users to sync their personal data of choice whether it be
41	from a personal wellness product or conversations from personal contacts into an artificially intelligent
42	chatbot that can refine an individual or couple’s relationship strengths and mitigate its weaknesses. As
43	Sync expands its user base, chatbots can study, learn, and predict better relationship standards for
44	
45	
46	individuals who are looking for a digital reference to build a relationship with. Giving individuals a chance to
47	understand themselves, and the special someone they find after.
